meta {
  name: 12 Get Effective Registration Settings
  type: http
  seq: 12
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/registration-settings/effective
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{businessAccessToken}}
}

tests {
  test("200 OK", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(200);
  });
  test("returns the active branch's full settings row", function () {
    const d = res.getBody().data;
    expect(d).to.have.property("branchId");
    expect(d).to.have.property("Patients_AllowB2bPatientWithoutMobile");
    expect(d).to.have.property("ChargesAndDeductions_AllowDiscounts");
    expect(d).to.have.property("Quotation_AutoIncrementExternalQuoteIdFormat");
    expect(d).to.have.property("EmergencyPricing_OverrideEmergencyPrices");
  });
}

docs {
  The active branch's Registration settings **as they apply** — the read the
  operational screens use (Create Order / Create Patient, Billings, Order
  Console, Quotations) to honour the saved toggles, e.g.
  `Patients_AllowB2bPatientWithoutMobile` makes Mobile optional on B2B orders.

  Login-only (no settings permission needed). The
  `registration:registration_settings__view_registration_settings` /
  `__update_registration_settings` permissions control who may open and change
  the Registration Settings page (`GET`/`PUT /registration-settings`), never
  whether the saved settings take effect — so a user without them still gets
  the real saved values here, not the defaults.

  Same row the backend enforces with (`getForBranch`): the branch's own row,
  created with defaults on first access. Tenant + branch come from the JWT /
  active profile. A caller with no active branch gets 404
  (`BRANCH_NOT_FOUND`), like `GET /registration-settings`.

  Response `data`: the full settings row (same shape as
  `GET /registration-settings`).
}
